# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mint Rewards Backend — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) for local work, and populate BOTH Vercel projects:
#
#   dev   →  api-dev.mintrewards.app          (tracks the `dev` branch)
#   prod  →  mint-rewards-backend.vercel.app  (tracks `main`)
#
# Every key below is REQUIRED unless marked OPTIONAL. lib/env.ts validates all
# of them at module load and fails with a single error listing everything that
# is missing or malformed — a deployment cannot boot half-configured.
#
# Markers:
#   [DIFFERS]  must hold a different value in dev vs prod
#   [SAME]     intentionally identical in both
#   [OPTIONAL] may be omitted; the default is inert
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Environment identity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Exactly "development" or "production". NOT derived from NODE_ENV:
# Vercel forces NODE_ENV=production on both projects, so NODE_ENV cannot tell
# the two deployments apart. This is the only thing that can.
APP_ENV=development


# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Separate Atlas databases. Sharing one defeats the entire split.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://USER:PASSWORD@cluster.example.mongodb.net/mint_rewards_dev

# [DIFFERS] Isolated test database. Required by `npm test`, `npm run dev:testdb`,
# and every script under scripts/ that writes data. Its database name must
# contain "test" or the seed scripts refuse to run.
MONGODB_URI_TEST=mongodb+srv://USER:PASSWORD@cluster.example.mongodb.net/test_db


# ── Consumer-app JWT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Minimum 16 characters. A dev-signed token must not authenticate
# against prod, so these must not match.
#
# NOTE: NEXTAUTH_SECRET and NEXT_JWT_SECRET are GONE. They were fallbacks in a
# three-deep lookup chain, not separate secrets. Signing algorithm and token
# payload are unchanged — only the lookup collapsed.
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string-min-16-chars

# [OPTIONAL][SAME] Token lifetime. Defaults to "7d". Inert — no resource behind it.
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d


# ── BrandHub JWT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Deliberately distinct from JWT_SECRET and ADMIN_JWT_SECRET so a
# token from one system can never validate in another. Minimum 16 characters.
BRANDHUB_JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-different-long-random-string


# ── Global admin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Minimum 16 characters.
ADMIN_JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-third-long-random-string

# [DIFFERS] Admin login email.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# [DIFFERS] bcrypt hash of the admin password — never the password itself.
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('bcryptjs').hashSync('PASSWORD',10))"
ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=$2b$10$replace.this.with.a.real.bcrypt.hash.value.here.xxxxx

# ── OTP ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] HMAC pepper for stored OTP hashes. Minimum 16 characters.
#
# WARNING: changing this invalidates every OTP already stored in that
# environment's database — pending password-reset and email-verification codes
# stop verifying. Rotate only when no codes are outstanding.
OTP_PEPPER=replace-with-a-long-random-pepper-min-16-chars


# ── Google Sign-In ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] The dev bundle ID needs its own iOS OAuth client.
GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-devxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# [SAME] The web client ID ID tokens are verified against. Shared unless you
# split the Google Cloud project.
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-webxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com


# ── Apple Sign-In ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Verified as the `aud` claim on the Apple identity token.
#   dev   → com.mintrewards.app.dev
#   prod  → com.mintrewards.app
#
# This key was previously read by the Apple route but defined NOWHERE — every
# Apple sign-in returned a 500. It is now required at boot, so a deployment
# missing it cannot start rather than failing silently at request time.
APPLE_BUNDLE_ID=com.mintrewards.app.dev


# ── Email (Resend) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Use a separate Resend key per environment so dev sending volume and
# suppressions never touch prod's reputation.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_with_your_resend_api_key

# [DIFFERS — see note] Sending identity. Was hardcoded in four files under
# emailServices/ as "Mint Rewards" <noreply@verify.mymintrewards.com>.
#
# Set this to a dev-only domain once one is verified in Resend. Until then dev
# still SENDS FROM the production identity — but it can no longer send TO real
# users, because DEV_MAIL_REDIRECT_TO below rewrites every recipient.
EMAIL_FROM="Mint Rewards" <noreply@verify.mymintrewards.com>

# [DIFFERS] Non-production mail sink. REQUIRED whenever APP_ENV is not
# "production", and REJECTED when it is — lib/env.ts fails the boot either way.
#
# Every outbound message is rewritten to this address regardless of its real
# recipient, so a dev deployment cannot email a real user. The original
# recipient is preserved in the subject: "[development -> user@example.com] ...".
#
# Applied in emailServices/emailFunction.ts, the single choke point all mail
# passes through — signup, password reset, verification codes, referrals.
DEV_MAIL_REDIRECT_TO=engineering@mymintrewards.com


# ── Storage (Vercel Blob) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [DIFFERS] Separate blob stores. Previously read with no validation, so an
# absent value silently fell through to the SDK's ambient BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN
# — which on Vercel could be a different store than intended.
BLOB_PUBLIC_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_replace_with_your_token


# ── CORS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated EXACT origins (scheme + host, no path, no trailing slash).
# No wildcards, no pattern matching, no preview-deployment support.
#
# [DIFFERS] — but note WHY the BrandHub entry is identical in both:
#
#   BrandHub has ONE deployment (https://mint-rewards-brandhub.vercel.app) and
#   no dev/prod split. It points at whichever backend its own VITE_API_URL
#   names. So BOTH backend projects allowlist that same origin BY DESIGN —
#   this is the intended architecture, not a stopgap. It stays this way unless
#   BrandHub itself is later split into separate dev/prod projects, at which
#   point each backend project takes only its counterpart's origin.
#
#   What DOES differ: only the dev project carries the local Vite dev server
#   origin. Prod must never allowlist a localhost origin.
#
# dev project:
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://mint-rewards-brandhub.vercel.app,http://localhost:5173
#
# prod project:
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://mint-rewards-brandhub.vercel.app


# ── Provided automatically by Vercel ─────────────────────────────────────────
# [OPTIONAL] VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA — surfaced by GET /api/health as `commit`.
# Do not set manually; absent locally, which is expected.
